<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92393" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥῑγ-έω</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>N.</u>
			5.50
		</span></i>: fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.351
				</span></i>
			: aor.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρρίγησα</span>, 
				Ep.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥίγησα</span> (also in <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1607
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.596
			</span></i>: pf. (with pres. sense) 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρρῑγα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					17.175
				</span></i>
			 (prob. f.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Ign.</u>
				74
			</span></i>); 
				Dor.
			
			3pl.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρρίγαντι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					16.77
				</span></i>
			; 
				Ep.
			
			subj.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρρίγῃσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.353
				</span></i>
			; 
				Ep.
			 dat. part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρρίγοντι</span> (for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρριγότι</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				228
			</span></i>: plpf.
			3sg.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρρίγει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					23.216
				</span></i>
			:—<i>shudder</i> or <i>bristle</i> with fear or
			horror, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδὼν ῥίγησε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.596
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρρίγησαν ὅπως ἴδον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					12.208
				</span></i>
			; once in Trag., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ δὲ παρθένοι
				ῥίγησαν</span> (the augm. being omitted although in an
			iambic verse) S.l.c.: c. inf., <i>shudder to do,
				shrink from doing</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄφρα τις ἐρρίγῃσι . . ξεινοδόκον κακὰ
					ῥέξαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.353
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				7.114
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπορριγέω</span>: folld. by
			a clause, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυμὸς ἐρρίγει μὴ . . </span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					23.216
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>cool</i> or <i>slacken in zeal</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				5.50
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>bristle</i> with arms, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φοίνικες . . ἐρρίγαντι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
				</span></i>
			 l.c. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<i>shudder at</i> anything, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥιγήσειν πόλεμον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.351
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔρριγα μάχην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					17.175
				</span></i>
			 (in <i><span class="en">
				16.119
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥίγησέν τε</span> is best taken
			parenthetically). (Cf. Lat. <i>frīgeo</i>, from
				<i>srīg-.</i>)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
